---
title: Cranberry sauce
servings: 7
yield: 2 1/4 cups
tags: [american, vegan, gluten-free, thanksgiving, holiday, fall, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
time: 15 minutes
source: Cranberry Sauce by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/cranberry-sauce.html
---

Bring the @water{1/2%cup}, @orange juice{1/2%cup}(fresh, from about 2 oranges) and @granulated sugar{14%tbsp}(3/4 cup plus 2 tbsp) to a boil in a #medium saucepan{} over high heat.

Add the @cranberries{12%oz}(fresh or frozen), finely grated zest of @orange{1}(about 2 tsp) and a pinch of @salt{}. Bring back to a boil.

Turn the heat to medium and simmer gently ~{10%minutes} to 12 minutes, until most of the berries have burst. Mash a few against the side if needed.

Spoon into a bowl, cover and chill.

> It keeps about 10 days in the fridge, or 2 months frozen.
